{"toolCallId":"call_c6bfec98ce654a34a6b659d42df1bdba","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"67:| `MEASURED_BEHAVIOR` | WARNING  | spec.md stamped v2.4+ | `measured-behavior` anchor present with the changed command's verbatim output, or an `N/A:` line with a reason |\n68-\n69-> **Partial reference:** The table above covers the most commonly-encountered rules. The authoritative, complete rule set and their canonical severities live in [`runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json`](../../runtime/cli/lib/validator-registry.json).\n70-\n71-### AC_CLOSURE\n72-\n73-`AC_CLOSURE` decides whether a packet may be closed. It is registered at ERROR severity and runs by default; set `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE=false` to opt out.\n74-\n75-**Rule ID:** `AC_CLOSURE`\n76-\n77-**Scope:** Levels 2, 3 and 3+. Level 1 keeps acceptance criteria inline in `spec.md` and is never gated.\n78-\n79-**Rollout:** forward-only behind `SPECKIT_AC_CLOSURE_CUTOFF` (default `2026-08-30`), compared against the `Created` date in the packet's `spec.md` metadata table. A packet created on or before the cutoff, or whose date cannot be read, is advisory on **every** branch — presence, waiver integrity and completion alike — and is never blocked. A malformed override falls back to the default rather than being compared as a string, which would otherwise grandfather the whole repository. This mirrors the `CANONICAL_SAVE_CUTOFF` pattern rather than introducing a third grandfathering mechanism.\n--\n132:### MEASURED_BEHAVIOR\n133-\n134:`MEASURED_BEHAVIOR` checks that `spec.md` carries the measurement a later reader needs to judge a claim about current behavior. It is registered at WARNING severity, so it never fails a run, `--strict` included.\n135-\n136:**Rule ID:** `MEASURED_BEHAVIOR`\n137-\n138-**Scope:** a `spec.md` whose `SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE` stamp names v2.4 or later. A doc with an older stamp, or none, is not checked.\n139-\n140-**The anchor:** `### Measured Behavior`, right after the problem section. The rule warns when that anchor is missing, and when its block holds neither a non-empty fenced command output nor an `N/A:` line with a reason.\n141-\n142-**Purpose:** the author pastes the command the feature changes and its verbatim output. Every number the spec states about current behavior quotes that block, so a reader reruns the command instead of trusting the prose.\n143-\n144-| Result | Meaning |\n145-|---|---|\n146-| `pass` | The anchor exists and its block holds a command output or an `N/A:` line with a reason |\n147-| `warn`, missing | No `measured-behavior` anchor in `spec.md` |\n148-| `warn`, empty | The block holds neither a command output nor a reasoned `N/A:` |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"91d82c","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
